{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/681626-how-do-you-honor-your-territory-in-all-things","id":681626,"title":"How do you honor your territory in all things","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-28T18:49:49-07:00","id":681626,"title":"How do you honor your territory in all things","content":"I like the oaths of the various tribes as reflections of their patron totem's ban. For the most part I understand how each defines the Tribe and acts as a duel edged sword. It is only &quot;Honor your territory in all things,&quot; that I have some trouble with especially with Red Wolf's capacity as agent (or at least chronicler) of change.<br /> <br /> I was hoping some examples might help me understand the Iron Master's ban a bit better.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","user":"Chris Wilson","date":". 09-28-2015, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T18:54:26-07:00","id":681651,"title":"","content":"Everything changes, but there's to be something of yours that is you. It doesn't have to be much, maybe a box o photos, or a bedroom. It's just &quot;yours&quot; and no one else's. <br /> <br /> It's a hard concept from the base wording, but the tribes of the moon book explains it lovely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T19:08:44-07:00","id":681657,"title":"","content":"The Tribes of the Moon book does get into it starting on page 133. The big thing is that the oath seems to be more of an anchor for the Iron Masters, who as you noted are followers of an agent of change. Getting them to honor their territory allows them focus. But just like the other oaths a lot is going to be up to individual interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T19:26:16-07:00","id":681683,"title":"","content":"Not sure what Tribes of the Moon says, but I have some thoughts on the subject. Like said, Red Wolf and his children understand change, and their Ban encompasses why they are the <i>Iron</i> Masters. The Farsil Luhal honor their territory by changing, by approaching the problem the way it wants to be approached. And in the modern world, problems often would rather be solved by a bit of cash &quot;gifted&quot; to the right person than a wolf-monster's growling visage, by the flash of a gun than the claws of the War-form. And so, the Iron Masters honor their territory, by playing according to the rules and milieu it demands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T19:26:55-07:00","id":681684,"title":"","content":"As mentioned, honoring your territory is a way of directing the change. The Masters could run a real risk of just anarchically chasing the dawn in a total case of neophilia, so they focus it down to what their territory does, or what the intended spirit of it is, and changing it in accordance to that idea.<br /> <br /> So, for example, if you have a part of town that became something special for the place it gave classic rockers and fans, and has continued to thrive in it's relationship to rock n' roll, than you can find new ways to improve the area by fostering community and solidarity in the music. You can expand it by bringing in new forms of rock that might be neglected but honor the spirit that started rock or the sounds that got it. Stuff like that<br /> <br /> What you cannot do is try and turn the area into a bastion of soft classical music just because it's making current cultural advances in today's society....except this leads into questions of how to interpret the vow. If Honoring Your Territory risks leaving it in the dust, can you really say you're honoring it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T02:20:25-07:00","id":681861,"title":"","content":"Don't shit where you eat, keep your room clean, and don't allow your territory to fall into decay or take actions that will cause it to become imbalanced. Basically &quot;think of the repercussions before you act, but don't wait to act until it's too late&quot;. That's the most simplistic way for me to explain it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:54:41-07:00","id":682224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/681626-how-do-you-honor-your-territory-in-all-things?p=681861#post681861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't shit where you eat, keep your room clean, and don't allow your territory to fall into decay or take actions that will cause it to become imbalanced. Basically &quot;think of the repercussions before you act, but don't wait to act until it's too late&quot;. That's the most simplistic way for me to explain it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bought the summary we can ask for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}